{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Subāhu","html":"<article id='thag1.52'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.52 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.52 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Chaṭṭhavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Six </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Subāhuttheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Subāhu </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Vassati devo yathā sugītaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The heavens rain like a sweet song; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Channā me kuṭikā sukhā nivātā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>my hut is roofed and pleasant, sheltered from the wind. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cittaṁ susamāhitañca kāye, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>My mind is immersed in my body: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha ce patthayasi pavassa devā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so rain forth, heavens, if you wish. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Subāhutthero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
